==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From the Indo-European root ''*man-'' (hand), which led to a Germanic base with a variety of meanings.  [[cognate|Cognates]] include Old Frisian ''mund'' ([[guardian]], [[guardianship]]), Old Saxon ''mund'' (hand), Old High German ''[[munt]]'' ([[hand]], [[protection]]), German ''[[Mund]], [[Munt]]'' ("legal power of protection"), Icelandic ''[[mundur]]'' ("a sum a bridegroom pays his bride").  The IE root was also the source of {{L.|lang=is}} ''[[manus]]'' ("[[hand]]"), Albanian ''[[marr]]'' ("turn").
===Noun===
'''mund''' {{f}}

# [[hand]]

====Derived terms====
*[[morgunstund gefur gull í mund]]

